From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0527 sweet_nub: print each child's USBDeviceFunction tag in the 5 s sample

0525 built the device tree (child[0] IOUSBDeviceConfigurator, child[1] IOUSBDeviceInterface,
child[2] IOUSBDeviceInterface) but the sample only printed class names. The NCM/Mux personalities
match IOUSBDeviceInterface on IOPropertyMatch {USBDeviceFunction: AppleUSBNCMControl|Data|Mux},
so whether the clients can ever attach depends on that tag being present -- and on this build the
only "USBDeviceFunction" string in the prelinked image is ours, i.e. Apple's createUSBDevice path
does not obviously set it by that name. Printing it per child answers that offline question with
one boot instead of guessing.

Prepared while the volume gate has booting frozen; NOT dispatched until the gate clears.

--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -491,8 +491,16 @@
 		while (OSObject *obj = children_it->getNextObject()) {
 			IOService *child = OSDynamicCast(IOService, obj);
 			if (child != NULL) {
-				printf("SWEET NUB: child[%d] %s\n", children,
-				    child->getMetaClass()->getClassName());
+				/* 0527: the NCM/Mux personalities match IOUSBDeviceInterface children on
+				 * IOPropertyMatch {USBDeviceFunction: AppleUSBNCMControl|Data|Mux}. Print it
+				 * here too: if the configurator built the children but the tag is missing,
+				 * the clients can never attach and the next fix is in the description, not
+				 * in the endpoint virtuals. */
+				OSString *fn = OSDynamicCast(OSString,
+				    child->getProperty("USBDeviceFunction"));
+				printf("SWEET NUB: child[%d] %s fn=%s\n", children,
+				    child->getMetaClass()->getClassName(),
+				    fn != NULL ? fn->getCStringNoCopy() : "(none)");
 			} else {
 				printf("SWEET NUB: child[%d] (non-IOService)\n", children);
 			}
